control -- optional argument for vFunctionP and vFunction
*********************************************************

Description
===========

By default this argument is set to 2. Whether it is equal to 2 the vFunctionP
and vFunction methods terminate after finding three "aligned" values
$\text{v}_\mathfrak{p}(I^k),\text{v}_\mathfrak{p}(I^{k+1}),\text{v}_\mathfrak{p
}(I^{k+2})$ of the $\text{v}_\mathfrak{p}$-function. That means that
$\text{v}_\mathfrak{p}(I^{k+1})-\text{v}_\mathfrak{p}(I^k)=\text{v}_\mathfrak{p
}(I^{k+2})-\text{v}_\mathfrak{p}(I^{k+1})$. By increasing its value, the
methods terminate after finding $\texttt{control}+1$ aligned values.

See also
========

  * *note vFunctionP: vFunctionP, -- compute the
    $\text{v}_\mathfrak{p}$-function of monomial ideal $I$
  * *note vFunction: vFunction, -- compute the $\text{v}$-function of monomial
    ideal $I$

Functions with optional argument named control:
===============================================

  * "vFunction(...,control=>...)"
  * "vFunctionP(...,control=>...)"

