reesMap -- compute the Rees map of $I$
**************************************

  * Usage: 
        reesMap I
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a homogeneous ideal of
        polynomial ring $S = \mathbb{K}[x_1,\ldots,x_n]$, $\mathbb{K}$ a field
  * Outputs:
      * g, a *note ring map: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,, the Rees map of $I$

Description
===========

Given a homogeneous ideal $I$, with minimal homogeneous generating set
$\{f_1,\dots,f_m\}$, this method yields the bigraded map $g:
\mathbb{K}[x_1,\dots,x_n,y_1,\dots,y_m] \to \mathbb{K}[x_1,\dots,x_n,t]$
defined by setting $g(x_i) = x_i$ for $1 \le i \le n$ and $g(y_j) = f_j t$ for
$1 \le j \le m$ and with $\text{bideg}(x_i) = (1,0)$ and $\text{bideg}(y_j) =
(\text{deg}(f_j), 1)$.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = QQ[x_1..x_3];                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x_1*x_2,x_1*x_3,x_2*x_3);                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of S                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : reesMap I                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = map (QQ[x ..x , t], QQ[x ..x , y ..y ], {x , x , x , x x t, x x t,      |
|              1   3          1   3   1   3     1   2   3   1 2    1 3        |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : RingMap QQ[x ..x , t] <-- QQ[x ..x , y ..y ]                            |
|                 1   3             1   3   1   3                             |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|x x t})                                                                      |
| 2 3                                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : S = QQ[x_1..x_4];                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : I = ideal(x_1^3*x_2+x_3^4,x_1+x_2+x_4,x_3^3);                           |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : Ideal of S                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : reesMap I                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|                                                               3       4     |
|o6 = map (QQ[x ..x , t], QQ[x ..x , y ..y ], {x , x , x , x , x x t + x t,   |
|              1   4          1   4   1   3     1   2   3   4   1 2     3     |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : RingMap QQ[x ..x , t] <-- QQ[x ..x , y ..y ]                            |
|                 1   4             1   4   1   3                             |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                  3                                                          |
|x t + x t + x t, x t})                                                       |
| 1     2     4    3                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use reesMap:
====================

  * "reesMap(Ideal)"

