vFunction -- compute the $\text{v}$-function of monomial ideal $I$
******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        vFunction I
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a monomial ideal of polynomial
        ring $S = \mathbb{K}[x_1,\ldots,x_n]$, $\mathbb{K}$ a field
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note control: control, => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default
        value 2, can be changed to increase reliability
  * Outputs:
      * l, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the first element represents the
        slope of the line, while the second represents the $y$-intercept

Description
===========

For $k\gg0$, the numerical function $k\mapsto\text{v}(I^k)$ is a linear
function of the form $mk+q$, with $m=\alpha(I)$ the initial degree of $I$ and
$q\ge-1$ an integer. This method computes the pair $(\alpha(I),q)$.

+----------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = QQ[x_1..x_3];                  |
+----------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x_1*x_2,x_1*x_3,x_2*x_3);|
|                                        |
|o2 : Ideal of S                         |
+----------------------------------------+
|i3 : vFunction I                        |
|                                        |
|o3 = {2, -1}                            |
|                                        |
|o3 : List                               |
+----------------------------------------+
|i4 : vFunction(I,control=>3)            |
|                                        |
|o4 = {2, -1}                            |
|                                        |
|o4 : List                               |
+----------------------------------------+
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : S = QQ[x_1..x_3];                                |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : I = ideal(x_1,x_2)*ideal(x_1,x_3)*ideal(x_2,x_3);|
|                                                      |
|o6 : Ideal of S                                       |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : vFunction I                                      |
|                                                      |
|o7 = {3, -1}                                          |
|                                                      |
|o7 : List                                             |
+------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note vNumber: vNumber, -- compute the $\text{v}$-number of homogeneous
    ideal $I$
  * *note vNumberP: vNumberP, -- compute the $\text{v}_\mathfrak{p}$-number of
    homogeneous ideal $I$
  * *note vFunctionP: vFunctionP, -- compute the
    $\text{v}_\mathfrak{p}$-function of monomial ideal $I$

Ways to use vFunction:
======================

  * "vFunction(Ideal)"

