vNumberP -- compute the $\text{v}_\mathfrak{p}$-number of homogeneous ideal $I$
*******************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        vNumberP(I,p)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a homogeneous ideal of
        polynomial ring $S = \mathbb{K}[x_1,\ldots,x_n]$, $\mathbb{K}$ a field
      * p, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a associated prime of $I$
  * Outputs:
      * k, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 

Description
===========

This method computes the $\text{v}_{\mathfrak{p}}$-number of $I$:
$$\text{v}_{\mathfrak{p}}(I)=\min\{\text{deg}(f):f\in S\ \text{is homogeneous,
and}\ (I:f)=\mathfrak{p}\}.$$

+---------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = QQ[x_1..x_3];                 |
+---------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x_1*x_2,x_1*x_3,x_2*x_3)|
|                                       |
|o2 = ideal (x x , x x , x x )          |
|             1 2   1 3   2 3           |
|                                       |
|o2 : Ideal of S                        |
+---------------------------------------+
|i3 : p = ideal(x_1,x_2)                |
|                                       |
|o3 = ideal (x , x )                    |
|             1   2                     |
|                                       |
|o3 : Ideal of S                        |
+---------------------------------------+
|i4 : vNumberP(I,p)                     |
|                                       |
|o4 = 1                                 |
+---------------------------------------+
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : S = QQ[x_1..x_4];                            |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : I = ideal(x_1^3*x_2+x_3^4,x_1+x_2+x_4,x_3^3);|
|                                                  |
|o6 : Ideal of S                                   |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : p = (ass I)#0;                               |
|                                                  |
|o7 : Ideal of S                                   |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : vNumberP(I,p)                                |
|                                                  |
|o8 = 5                                            |
+--------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note vNumber: vNumber, -- compute the $\text{v}$-number of homogeneous
    ideal $I$
  * *note vFunctionP: vFunctionP, -- compute the
    $\text{v}_\mathfrak{p}$-function of monomial ideal $I$
  * *note vFunction: vFunction, -- compute the $\text{v}$-function of monomial
    ideal $I$

Ways to use vNumberP:
=====================

  * "vNumberP(Ideal,Ideal)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note vNumberP: vNumberP, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

